   "source": [
    "# 37. What’s the difference between probability and likelihood?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "c20c0061",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This is one of the most commonly asked ML/statistics interview questions.\n",
    "\n",
    "🎯 Core Idea\n",
    "Aspect\tProbability\tLikelihood\n",
    "Meaning\tChance of observing data given parameters\tHow likely parameters are given observed data\n",
    "Known\tParameters are fixed\tData is fixed\n",
    "Variable\tData varies\tParameters vary\n",
    "Used for\tPrediction\tParameter estimation\n",
    "📌 Mathematical Perspective\n",
    "\n",
    "For a coin toss:\n",
    "\n",
    "P(X∣θ)=θ\n",
    "x\n",
    "(1−θ)\n",
    "n−x\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "\n",
    "θ = probability of heads\n",
    "X = observed data\n",
    "✅ In Probability\n",
    "θ is fixed\n",
    "We calculate probability of data\n",
    "\n",
    "👉 Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "If coin is fair (θ=0.5)\n",
    "What is probability of getting 4 heads?\n",
    "✅ In Likelihood\n",
    "Data is already observed\n",
    "We estimate best θ\n",
    "\n",
    "👉 Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "Observed: H H H T H\n",
    "What value of θ most likely generated this?\n",
    "🧠 Simple Intuition\n",
    "🔹 Probability\n",
    "\n",
    "👉 “What can happen?”\n",
    "\n",
    "🔹 Likelihood\n",
    "\n",
    "👉 “What parameter best explains what already happened?”\n",
    "\n",
    "🚀 In Machine Learning\n",
    "🔹 Probability\n",
    "\n",
    "Used in:\n",
    "\n",
    "Prediction\n",
    "Bayesian methods\n",
    "Classification\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "P(y∣x)\n",
    "🔹 Likelihood\n",
    "\n",
    "Used in:\n",
    "\n",
    "Model training\n",
    "Maximum Likelihood Estimation (MLE)\n",
    "\n",
    "Goal:\n",
    "\n",
    "Find parameters maximizing likelihood\n",
    "🔥 Interview Trick\n",
    "\n",
    "👉 Probability and likelihood may use the same formula, but interpretation changes depending on:\n",
    "\n",
    "What is fixed\n",
    "What varies\n",
    "🎯 Interview-Ready Answer (Perfect)**\n",
    "\n",
    "👉 “Probability measures the chance of observing data given known parameters, while likelihood measures how likely certain parameters are given observed data. In probability, parameters are fixed and data varies; in likelihood, data is fixed and parameters vary.”\n",
    "\n",
    "🔥 Pro Tip\n",
    "\n",
    "👉 Say this line to impress interviewer:\n",
    "\n",
    "👉 “Likelihood is not a probability distribution over parameters—it is a function of parameters given observed data.”"
   ]
  },
